<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API. Do not paste this back into
        <description>. NOTE ALSO: the comment must sit INSIDE the root element - a comment
        placed ABOVE <ValidationRule> breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        THE ALL-SIGNED RELEASE GATE. Nothing is released to a prospective buyer until every NDA
        collected against that disposition reads Signed. Source: Part 2 line 305, "nothing is
        released until this is done".

        IT BLOCKS EVERY FORWARD STAGE FROM NDA ONWARD, NOT JUST THE NEXT HOP (decision D15/Q4).
        Disposition_Stage__c is freely settable - the No_Backward_Stage_Movement rule is
        Opportunity-only and nothing stops a user jumping NDA -> LOI directly. Gating only the
        NDA -> Release Materials hop would therefore be a gate a single click bypasses, so the
        rule names Release Materials, Active Listing, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing AND
        Sale Closes. A future stage added after NDA must be added to this OR list explicitly; it
        is NOT covered automatically. Same maintenance contract as
        Opportunity.NDA_Signed_Before_Deal_Progression, which carries the identical warning.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 RETRACTED 2026-08-19 - THE RECORD-TYPE TERM IS GONE AND THIS RULE NOW GOVERNS BOTH
        PATHS. THE PARAGRAPH THAT REQUIRED THE TERM IS QUOTED AND RETRACTED, NOT DELETED.
        =====================================================================================

            RETRACTED: "WHY THE RECORD-TYPE TEST IS REQUIRED. Four of the five gated stages -
            LOI, PSA, Closing, Completed - are SHARED with the on-market path, where NDAs are
            not collected at all and this gate must never fire. Only Disposition Offer and NDA
            are off-market-only. So unlike a value-set-disjoint rule, this one cannot be
            self-limiting by stage value and needs an explicit record-type criterion."

            ALSO RETRACTED, from the paragraph above it: "On an OFF-MARKET disposition, nothing
            is released ..." - the scope word "OFF-MARKET" is what died, not the rule.

        WHY IT DIED - THE PREMISE, NOT THE PRINCIPLE. The retracted paragraph was right that the
        rule cannot be self-limiting by stage value. Its premise was that NDAs "are not collected
        at all" on the on-market path. The client's 2026-08-19 redefinition makes NDA A STAGE ON
        BOTH PATHS: an on-market deal now collects NDAs from interested parties before materials
        are released, exactly as an off-market one does. The gate must therefore fire on BOTH
        record types, and the term that scoped it to one is not merely unnecessary - it would
        actively DISABLE the gate on the path that now has the larger buyer population.

        ⚠ THE SUBSTITUTION NOTE THAT SAT HERE IS ALSO OBSOLETE and is dropped rather than
        retracted, because it described syntax that no longer appears in the formula: the file
        used RecordType.DeveloperName instead of the $RecordType global, per Salesforce's "Tips
        for Referencing Record Types in Formulas". There is no record-type reference left below.
        The same substitution is still live in Disposition__c.Is_On_Market__c, which is where
        that guidance now applies.

        WHY ISCHANGED ONLY - DELIBERATELY DIVERGING FROM ITS SIBLING
        Wire_Complete_Before_Sale_Closes, which uses OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(...)). The test
        surface creates dispositions DIRECTLY at LOI and PSA to exercise those features, and
        ISNEW() would block its own fixtures. DispositionService is the only production creator
        and always creates at Disposition Readiness, so the create path is not a real exposure.
        THE RESIDUAL IS REAL AND IS ACCEPTED: creating a disposition directly at a later stage
        bypasses this gate entirely.

        WHY BLANKVALUE. NDA_Count__c and Signed_NDA_Count__c carry defaultValue 0, but a default
        applies only at INSERT - every Disposition__c row that existed before those fields were
        created holds NULL. A null Number in a comparison makes the whole expression null, which
        a validation rule treats as FALSE - so the naive form NDA_Count__c = 0 would FAIL OPEN on
        exactly the pre-existing rows, letting a disposition with no NDAs at all sail past the
        gate. BLANKVALUE(...,0) makes both terms total. Do not "simplify" it away.

        NDA_Count__c = 0 IS A BLOCKING CONDITION, NOT AN OVERSIGHT. A disposition on which NO NDA
        was ever collected must not advance: collecting nothing is not the same as collecting
        everything. That is also why the rollup maintains TWO counts rather than one unsigned
        count, which would read 0 in both situations.

        🔴 A DECLINED NDA NO LONGER BLOCKS - AMENDED 2026-08-09 BY DECISION D20/C2, AND THE
        FORMULA DID NOT CHANGE THEN EITHER. The superseded paragraph is quoted and retracted
        rather than deleted, because it is the reasoning a future reader is most likely to try to
        restore:

            RETRACTED: "A DECLINED NDA STILL BLOCKS. It counts toward the total and not toward
            the signed count, so the party exists and has not signed. If a party is genuinely
            out of the process the NDA record is DELETED, not left Declined - which is stated
            in the Declined step of NDA_Path_Disposition."

        WHY IT WAS WRONG: it made Declined a state with NO USER-CLEARABLE EXIT. The fix is
        arithmetic and it lives in the COUNTER: NDA_Signed_Rollup's Is_Row_Signed decision counts
        a Declined row toward NEITHER counter, so a declined party is neither outstanding nor
        signed. THE EXCLUSION COULD NOT HAVE BEEN PUT IN THIS RULE: the formula below sees two
        Numbers on the parent and has no access to child rows at all - NDA__c.Disposition__c is a
        Lookup, not Master-Detail, so there is no roll-up summary available and a validation rule
        cannot count children.

        ⚠ TWO CONSEQUENCES OF THAT ARITHMETIC, BOTH INTENDED: a disposition whose ONLY NDA is
        Declined records NDA_Count__c = 0, and the first clause below STILL BLOCKS IT - which is
        precisely why that clause is not an oversight. And a disposition where the buyer declined
        but the introducing broker signed now PASSES: this gate governs the DISPOSITION's stage,
        and a party who declined "goes no further" (Part 2 line 231) while the disposition itself
        may still proceed with another buyer.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. The NDA_Signed_Rollup flow MUST already be deployed.
        Deploying this rule against no rollup leaves both counters at 0 or null with nothing able
        to set them, so NO disposition could advance past the NDA stage at all.

        FIRING SURFACE - DISPOSITION_STAGE__C NOW HAS THREE WRITERS, AND THIS RULE EVALUATES
        AGAINST ALL THREE.
          1. USER EDITS: the Path, the Details section, inline edit, and now the four
             Advance_to_* quick actions via RecordStageAdvanceService.
          2. ContractExecutionService.advanceDispositionsToClosing, which writes 'Closing' when
             a sell-side PSA reaches Executed. UNCHANGED by this tranche.
          3. NEW 2026-08-19: DispositionApprovalAdvanceQueueable, the D-1 approval auto-advance,
             which writes BOV Outreach / Broker Selection / NDA / Sale Closes, plus
             DispositionApprovalService.selectOffer, which writes 'Offer Selection', and the two
             child triggers, which write 'Broker Selection' and 'LOI'.
        🔴 FOUR OF THOSE MACHINE-WRITTEN TARGETS ARE IN THE OR LIST BELOW: Offer Selection, LOI,
        Closing and Sale Closes. THAT IS CORRECT AND MUST STAY - an approved offer or an executed
        PSA does not entitle a sale to skip the release gate. Every one of those writes is
        Database.update(..., false, AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE): SYSTEM_MODE bypasses CRUD and FLS,
        NOT validation rules, and allOrNone = false means this rule's refusal cannot roll back the
        approval, the Contract Review's Executed status or the notifications. What you get is a
        VISIBLE disagreement - an approved thing next to a stage that did not move - which any
        user can resolve by signing the outstanding NDAs and advancing by hand. Do not "repair"
        it by relaxing this gate and do not bypass validation on the Apex write.
        ⚠ FOR THE D-1 PATH SPECIFICALLY: a refusal leaves Approval_Advance_Pending__c TRUE. That
        is deliberate - the stuck record is findable by SOQL on that flag.

        BLAST RADIUS - for the developer and testing agents. THIS IS WIDER THAN BEFORE. Any test,
        seed script or fixture that moves ANY disposition - on-market included, which was
        previously exempt - to Release Materials, Active Listing, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA,
        Closing or Sale Closes now needs a signed NDA on it first. The three live On_Market rows
        at Active Listing and the two at Closing are in scope the moment anyone advances them.
    -->
    <fullName>All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>BOTH record types: blocks every forward stage from NDA onward (Release Materials, Active Listing, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes) until every non-Declined NDA on this disposition is Signed. Counts come from NDA_Signed_Rollup.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(Disposition_Stage__c),
    OR(
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Release Materials&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Active Listing&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Offer Selection&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;LOI&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;PSA&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Closing&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Disposition_Stage__c, &apos;Sale Closes&apos;)
    ),
    OR(
        BLANKVALUE(NDA_Count__c, 0) = 0,
        BLANKVALUE(Signed_NDA_Count__c, 0) &lt; BLANKVALUE(NDA_Count__c, 0)
    )
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Disposition_Stage__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>Every NDA on this disposition must be signed before information is released. Add the buyer&apos;s NDA (and the introducing broker&apos;s, if there is one) and mark each one Signed before advancing.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
